<title>UK: UK's Clarke says on course to double PFI deals.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke says on course to double PFI deals.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor Kenneth Clarke said on Tuesday the UK was on course to double the value of infrastructure spending under its Private Finance Initiative by March 1999.</p>
<p>In his budget presentation, Clarke said, &quot;A year ago we had agreed 1.5 billion pounds worth of (PFI) deals -- now we have agreed seven billion and we are on course to double that by March 1999.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 2274</p>
